# Chapter 1: Awakening
# The player wakes up in a damaged cryo pod

intro:
    bg none
    
    characterA ???
    t ...ystem reboot... emergency protocol...
    t ...vital signs detected... initiating revival sequence...
    
    fade 1.0
    
    bg cryo_room.png
    music ambient_ship.ogg
    
    characterA Protagonist
    moodA weak
    t Ugh... my head...
    t It feels like someone filled my skull with broken glass.
    t Where am I? Everything hurts.
    
    
    t The air is cold. Too cold. And there's a smell...
    t Burnt plastic. Ozone. Something else I don't want to identify.
    
    
    t I try to move, but my limbs feel like lead.
    t How long have I been asleep?
    
    characterB AI
    t Crew member detected. Initiating status report.
    t Please remain calm. Your body is recovering from extended cryogenic stasis.
    t You have been in cryogenic stasis for approximately 847 days.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t 847 days?! That's... over two years!
    t That can't be right. The mission was only supposed to be 6 months!
    
    characterB AI
    t Correct. The original mission parameters have been... significantly altered.
    t Emergency revival was triggered due to critical ship damage.
    t Life support failing. Estimated time remaining: 45 minutes.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t 45 minutes? That's all I have?
    t This has to be some kind of nightmare.
    
    characterB AI
    t I assure you, this situation is very real.
    t I recommend focusing on survival. I will assist you.
    
    branch What do you do?
        ask_ship Ask about the ship
        ask_crew Ask about the crew
        cryo_exit Look for an exit immediately

ask_ship:
    characterA Protagonist
    t What happened to the ship?
    t Why am I waking up two years late?
    
    characterB AI
    t The USV Meridian suffered a catastrophic collision with uncharted debris.
    t The debris field was not on any navigational charts.
    t Initial impact occurred 847 days, 14 hours, and 23 minutes ago.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t A debris field? In deep space?
    
    characterB AI
    t Hull breaches detected on decks 3 through 7. Primary reactor offline.
    t Backup power at 12% and declining.
    t The ship has been slowly dying since the collision.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Slowly dying... for over two years?
    t Is there any way to fix it?
    
    characterB AI
    t Negative. Structural integrity is compromised beyond repair.
    t I have been maintaining minimal life support while searching for survivors.
    t You are the first to revive successfully.
    t Recommended course of action: evacuation via escape pod.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t The first to revive... what about the others?
    
    characterB AI
    t ...
    t We should focus on your evacuation.
    
    goto cryo_exit

ask_crew:
    characterA Protagonist
    t What about the rest of the crew?
    t There were 24 of us. Where is everyone?
    
    characterB AI
    t ...
    
    
    t I have been dreading this question.
    t Of the 24 crew members aboard, you are the only survivor.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t What? No, that's... that's impossible!
    
    characterB AI
    t Cryo pod malfunctions claimed 19 lives.
    t The power fluctuations from the collision caused cascade failures.
    t I tried to reroute power, but I could not save them all.
    t I could barely save you.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t And the remaining 4?
    
    characterB AI
    t Their life signs terminated during the initial collision.
    t Captain Reyes was on the bridge. Engineer Tanaka in the reactor room.
    t Doctors Chen and Vasquez in the medical wing.
    t They died instantly. I... I am sorry. I was unable to protect them.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Captain Reyes... Tanaka... 
    t I knew them. I had dinner with them the night before we went into cryo.
    t ...I see.
    
    characterB AI
    t I understand if you need a moment.
    t But time is limited. We must proceed.
    
    goto cryo_exit

cryo_exit:
    characterA Protagonist
    t I need to find the escape pod. Where is it?
    t Just tell me where to go.
    
    characterB AI
    t Escape pod bay is located on Deck 2, Section C.
    t Under normal circumstances, it would be a 3 minute walk.
    t However... Warning: Direct route is blocked by debris.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Of course it is. What are my options?
    
    characterB AI
    t I have analyzed the structural integrity of all possible paths.
    t You will need to navigate through the cargo bay or the medical wing.
    t Both routes carry some risk, but they are passable.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Great. A choice between bad and worse.
    
    characterB AI
    t I will guide you regardless of which path you choose.
    t You will not be alone.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t ...Thanks. I think I needed to hear that.
    
    branch Which route do you take?
        cargo_entrance Go through the Cargo Bay
        medical_entrance Go through the Medical Wing
        search_cryo Search the cryo room first

search_cryo:
    bg cryo_room.png
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Maybe I should look around here first. There might be something useful.
    t I can't just rush into this unprepared.
    
    
    t The cryo room is a mess. Frost covers everything.
    t Some of the monitoring equipment is sparking.
    
    t The other cryo pods... they're all dark. Empty.
    t No, not empty. I can see shadows inside some of them.
    
    
    t I shouldn't look too closely.
    t I don't want to see their faces. I knew these people.
    
    
    t Focus. I need to survive. For them if not for myself.
    
    
    t There's a locker by the wall. Standard emergency kit.
    t The lock is broken, probably from the impact.
    
    # Player finds a flashlight
    t A flashlight. Still has some charge. This could be useful.
    t And a small tool kit. Might come in handy.
    
    characterB AI
    t I recommend proceeding to the escape pod bay. Time is limited.
    t You now have 38 minutes remaining.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Right. No more delays.
    
    branch Which route do you take?
        cargo_entrance Go through the Cargo Bay
        medical_entrance Go through the Medical Wing
